    59	            // `RemoteEndpoint::parse` bails "input appears to be a
    60	            // local path" when `check_local_path` recognizes a local
    61	            // path — including Windows drive paths (`C:/path`,
    62	            // `C:\path`) whose `:/` would otherwise trip the
    63	            // remote-shaped-typo guard below. Honor that lower-level
    64	            // classification: it's local, not a typo'd remote.
    65	            if err_msg.contains("appears to be a local path") {
    66	                // D-2026-08-20-3: still name the daemon-address trap —
    67	                // `1.2.3.4:9911//x/` lands here (the `:` is followed by
    68	                // a digit, so `check_local_path` calls it local), and
    69	                // silently creating a `./1.2.3.4:9911/` directory is
    70	                // exactly the footgun. Warn, don't refuse.
